<!DOCTYPE html>
{{- /*
  privacy.html.tmpl — the public privacy notice, server-rendered.

  Receives privacyData from internal/server/privacy.go. Like the
  profile page it carries no JavaScript: the opt-out control is a
  plain form POST, so it works with scripting disabled and cannot
  itself become a tracking surface.

  This page deliberately does NOT load web fonts, even when the
  profile page is configured to. Reading a privacy notice — and using
  the opt-out on it — should never cost you a request to a third
  party. The system font stacks in styles.css cover it.

  Everything factual here is generated from live config, so the
  notice describes what the site actually loads rather than
  boilerplate that drifts out of date as settings change.
*/ -}}
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
<title>Privacy Notice{{if .Meta.Title}} &middot; {{.Meta.Title}}{{end}}</title>
<meta name="description" content="How this site handles your information, and how to opt out of non-essential tracking." />
<link rel="icon" href="{{if .Meta.Favicon}}{{.Meta.Favicon}}{{else}}/static/favicon.svg{{end}}" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/styles.css" />
<style>
  /* System stacks only — see the note at the top of this file. */
  :root {
    --font-display: "Iowan Old Style", Palatino, Georgia, serif;
    --font-body: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    --font-mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main class="page page-prose">

  <nav class="prose-back">
    <a href="/">&larr; {{if .Profile.Name}}{{.Profile.Name}}{{else}}Back{{end}}</a>
  </nav>

  <header class="prose-head">
    <h1 class="prose-title">Privacy Notice</h1>
    <p class="prose-sub">
      {{- if .HasOperator}}For the site operated by {{.Privacy.Operator}}.{{else}}For this site.{{end}}
      {{- if .Privacy.Effective}} Effective {{.Privacy.Effective}}.{{end}}
    </p>
  </header>

  {{- /* ── The actionable part, first. ────────────────────────── */ -}}
  <section class="privacy-choices" id="choices">
    <h2 class="prose-h2">Your Privacy Choices</h2>

    {{- if eq .Saved "out"}}
    <p class="privacy-flash" role="status">Saved. Non-essential tracking is off for this browser.</p>
    {{- else if eq .Saved "in"}}
    <p class="privacy-flash" role="status">Saved. Non-essential tracking is allowed for this browser.</p>
    {{- end}}

    {{- if not .HasNonEssential}}
    <p>
      This site does not run analytics or advertising, and makes no
      third-party requests for them, so there is nothing here to turn
      off. The cookies it can set are listed below.
    </p>

    {{- else if .GPCActive}}
    <p class="privacy-state privacy-state-out">
      <strong>Your browser is sending a Global Privacy Control signal, and we have applied it.</strong>
      Non-essential tracking is switched off for this visit. You do not
      need to do anything else, and we will not ask you to confirm it.
    </p>
    {{- template "optOutForm" .}}

    {{- else if .DNTActive}}
    <p class="privacy-state privacy-state-out">
      <strong>Your browser is sending a Do Not Track header, and we have applied it.</strong>
      Non-essential tracking is switched off for this visit.
    </p>
    {{- template "optOutForm" .}}

    {{- else}}
    <p class="privacy-state{{if .OptedOut}} privacy-state-out{{else}} privacy-state-in{{end}}">
      {{- if .OptedOut}}
      <strong>Non-essential tracking is currently off</strong> for this browser, because you asked for it to be.
      {{- else}}
      <strong>Non-essential tracking is currently on</strong> for this browser. You can turn it off below.
      {{- end}}
    </p>
    {{- template "optOutForm" .}}
    {{- end}}

    {{- if .HasNonEssential}}
    <p class="prose-small">
      Your choice is remembered in a cookie on this browser for one
      year. It is not tied to an account and does not identify you, so
      clearing your cookies or switching browsers or devices will reset
      it. Opting out never changes what you can see or do on this site.
    </p>
    {{- end}}
  </section>

  {{- /* ── Disclosures. ───────────────────────────────────────── */ -}}
  <h2 class="prose-h2">What this site collects</h2>
  <p>
    This is a personal links page. There is no account to create, no
    form to fill in, and nothing here asks you for your name, address,
    payment details, or any other personal information.
  </p>
  <p>
    The software serving this page keeps a short technical log of each
    request &mdash; the method, the path requested, the response status,
    and the number of bytes sent. That log does not include your IP
    address. The web server, reverse proxy, or tunnel provider sitting
    in front of this site may keep its own logs, which typically do
    record IP addresses, and those are outside this application.
  </p>
  {{- if .SaleOrShare}}
  <p>
    Because this site loads an advertising component (described below),
    information about your visit may be disclosed to that provider in a
    way that counts as &ldquo;selling&rdquo; or &ldquo;sharing&rdquo;
    personal information under California law, and as
    &ldquo;targeted advertising&rdquo; under other state laws. Use the
    control above to opt out.
  </p>
  {{- end}}

  <h2 class="prose-h2">Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The site itself sets these two cookies, and no others. Neither is used
    for advertising.
  </p>
  <div class="prose-table-wrap">
    <table class="prose-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>linkhub_privacy_optout</code></td>
          <td>Remembers the privacy choice you make above. Set only once you use that control.</td>
          <td>1 year</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>linkhub_session</code></td>
          <td>Signs the site owner in to the private admin page. Set only after a successful login at <code>/login</code> &mdash; visitors browsing this site never receive it.</td>
          <td>12 hours</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="prose-small">
    Both are strictly necessary: one exists only to honor your own
    choice, the other only to keep the owner signed in. Neither is
    shared with anyone.
    {{- if ne .SnippetCategory "none"}}
    A third-party component is also loaded on the profile page (see
    below) and may set cookies of its own, under its provider&rsquo;s
    control rather than ours.
    {{- end}}
  </p>

  <h2 class="prose-h2">Who else receives data</h2>
  {{- if .GoogleFontsConfigured}}
  <p>
    <strong>Google Fonts.</strong> The profile page loads its typefaces
    from Google&rsquo;s font servers. Making that request discloses your
    IP address and browser user-agent string to Google. It sets no
    cookies.
    {{- if .GoogleFontsActive}}
    This request is active for you right now; opting out above stops it,
    and the page falls back to fonts already on your device.
    {{- else}}
    Because you have opted out, this request is not being made &mdash;
    the page is using fonts already on your device instead.
    {{- end}}
  </p>
  {{- end}}

  {{- if eq .SnippetCategory "analytics"}}
  <p>
    <strong>{{if .Privacy.SnippetDescription}}{{.Privacy.SnippetDescription}}{{else}}An analytics component{{end}}.</strong>
    The profile page loads this to measure traffic.
    {{- if .SnippetSuppressed}}
    Because you have opted out, it is not being loaded for you.
    {{- else}}
    It is active for you right now; opting out above stops it from loading.
    {{- end}}
  </p>
  {{- else if eq .SnippetCategory "advertising"}}
  <p>
    <strong>{{if .Privacy.SnippetDescription}}{{.Privacy.SnippetDescription}}{{else}}An advertising component{{end}}.</strong>
    The profile page loads this for advertising or audience-measurement
    purposes, and it may receive information about your visit.
    {{- if .SnippetSuppressed}}
    Because you have opted out, it is not being loaded for you.
    {{- else}}
    It is active for you right now; opting out above stops it from loading.
    {{- end}}
  </p>
  {{- else if eq .SnippetCategory "essential"}}
  <p>
    <strong>{{if .Privacy.SnippetDescription}}{{.Privacy.SnippetDescription}}{{else}}A required component{{end}}.</strong>
    The profile page loads this because the site needs it to function.
    It is not used for analytics or advertising, and it is not affected
    by the opt-out above.
  </p>
  {{- end}}

  {{- if and (not .GoogleFontsConfigured) (eq .SnippetCategory "none")}}
  <p>
    Nobody. This site makes no third-party requests: everything the page
    needs is served from this server.
  </p>
  {{- end}}

  <p>
    The links on the profile page point to other websites. Following one
    takes you to a service with its own privacy practices, which this
    notice does not cover.
  </p>

  <h2 class="prose-h2">How long information is kept</h2>
  <p>
    {{- if .Privacy.Retention}}
    {{.Privacy.Retention}}
    {{- else}}
    Request logs are kept only as long as they are useful for operating
    and debugging the site, and are not used to build any profile of
    you. No visitor database exists, because no visitor information is
    collected into one.
    {{- end}}
  </p>

  <h2 class="prose-h2">Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, state law may give you the right to
    know what personal information a business has collected about you,
    to get a copy of it, to correct it, to have it deleted, and to opt
    out of its sale, sharing, or use for targeted advertising. You also
    have the right not to be treated differently for exercising any of
    these rights &mdash; and nothing on this site changes based on the
    choice you make above.
  </p>
  <p>
    In practice there is very little to request here: this site holds no
    account for you and builds no profile of you. The opt-out control
    above is the meaningful one, and it takes effect immediately.
  </p>
  {{- if .HasContact}}
  <p>
    To make a request, or to ask anything about this notice, contact
    <a class="prose-link" href="{{.ContactHref}}">{{.Privacy.Contact}}</a>.
    You may also have someone act on your behalf; we may need to confirm
    with you before acting on such a request.
  </p>
  {{- else}}
  <p class="privacy-warn">
    The operator of this site has not published a contact address for
    privacy requests yet. Until they do, requests can be made through
    any contact channel listed on the main page.
  </p>
  {{- end}}

  <h2 class="prose-h2">Global Privacy Control</h2>
  <p>
    This site recognizes and honors the
    <a class="prose-link" href="https://globalprivacycontrol.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Global Privacy Control</a>
    signal. If your browser or an extension sends
    <code>Sec-GPC: 1</code>, we treat it as a valid opt-out on every
    request, automatically, without asking you to confirm and without
    showing you a banner. We honor the older <code>DNT: 1</code> header
    the same way.
  </p>
  <p class="prose-small">
    Twelve states &mdash; California, Colorado, Connecticut, Delaware,
    Maryland, Minnesota, Montana, Nebraska, New Hampshire, New Jersey,
    Oregon, and Texas &mdash; require sites to recognize a universal
    opt-out signal of this kind. Our machine-readable declaration is at
    <a class="prose-link" href="/.well-known/gpc.json"><code>/.well-known/gpc.json</code></a>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="prose-h2">Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    This notice is generated from the site&rsquo;s live configuration,
    so it reflects what the site loads at the moment you read it. If the
    operator turns tracking on or off, this page changes with it.
  </p>

  <footer class="footer prose-foot">
    <p class="footer-line">
      {{- if .Footer.ShowYear}}&copy; {{.Year}}{{end}}
      {{- if and .Footer.ShowYear .Footer.Text}} &middot; {{end}}
      {{- if .Footer.Text}}{{.Footer.Text}}{{end}}
    </p>
    <p class="footer-privacy"><a class="privacy-link" href="/">Back to the profile</a></p>
  </footer>

</main>
</body>
</html>

{{- /* ── The opt-out control itself. ──────────────────────────────
       Two submit buttons in one form, distinguished by value. No
       JavaScript, no fetch, no client-side state: the server reads
       the posted value, writes the cookie, and redirects back here.
       Rendered as a named template because three branches above use
       it and they must stay identical. */ -}}
{{- define "optOutForm"}}
<form class="privacy-form" method="post" action="/privacy/choices">
  <button class="privacy-btn privacy-btn-out{{if .OptedOut}} is-current{{end}}"
          type="submit" name="choice" value="optout">
    Opt out of non-essential tracking
  </button>
  <button class="privacy-btn privacy-btn-in{{if not .OptedOut}} is-current{{end}}"
          type="submit" name="choice" value="allow">
    Allow non-essential tracking
  </button>
</form>
{{- if .GPCActive}}
<p class="prose-small">
  While your browser keeps sending the Global Privacy Control signal it
  overrides whichever button you press &mdash; the signal is the
  stronger instruction and we treat it that way. What you choose here is
  still recorded, and takes over if you later turn the signal off.
</p>
{{- else if .DNTActive}}
<p class="prose-small">
  While your browser keeps sending the Do Not Track header it overrides
  whichever button you press. What you choose here is still recorded,
  and takes over if you later turn the header off.
</p>
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
